IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: ACTS CAUSING OR TENDING TO CAUSE
-- DANGER TO LIFE OR BODILY HARM, THIRD GROUP (sections 32 to 35): railways, and
-- vehicles.
--
-- "unlawfully", "maliciously", "wilfully", "wanton", "furious": none is defined in the
-- text; each is a fact the person states.  Sections 34 and 35 have no intent element.

§ `Acts causing or tending to cause Danger to Life or Bodily Harm: sections 32 to 35`

§§ `Section 32: placing wood, &c., on a railway, with intent to endanger passengers`

-- src:52 | 32 Placing wood, &c., on a railway, with intent to endanger passengers.
-- src:53 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously put or throw upon or across any railway any wood, stone, or other matter or thing, or shall unlawfully and maliciously take up, remove, or displace any rail, sleeper, or other matter or thing belonging to any railway, or shall unlawfully and maliciously turn, move, or divert any points or other machinery belonging to any railway, or shall unlawfully and maliciously make or show, hide or remove, any signal or light upon or near to any railway, or shall unlawfully and maliciously do or cause to be done any other matter or thing, with intent, in any of the cases aforesaid, to endanger the safety of any person travelling or being upon such railway, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be kept in penal servitude for life . . . or to be imprisoned . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 32 (src:52-53)
-- Five ways of acting, each introduced in the text by "shall unlawfully and
-- maliciously": (1) put or throw upon or across any railway wood, stone or other
-- matter or thing; (2) take up, remove or displace any rail, sleeper or other matter
-- or thing belonging to any railway; (3) turn, move or divert any points or other
-- machinery belonging to any railway; (4) make or show, hide or remove, any signal or
-- light upon or near to any railway; (5) do or cause to be done any other matter or
-- thing.  And an intent "in any of the cases aforesaid": to endanger the safety of
-- any person travelling or being upon the railway.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 32` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `put or threw upon or across a railway wood, stone or other matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took up, removed or displaced a rail, sleeper or other matter or thing belonging to a railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `turned, moved or diverted points or other machinery belonging to a railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made or showed, hid or removed a signal or light upon or near to a railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did or caused to be done any other matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to endanger the safety of a person travelling or being upon the railway` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 32 (src:53)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 32`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND (   c's `put or threw upon or across a railway wood, stone or other matter or thing`
         OR c's `took up, removed or displaced a rail, sleeper or other matter or thing belonging to a railway`
         OR c's `turned, moved or diverted points or other machinery belonging to a railway`
         OR c's `made or showed, hid or removed a signal or light upon or near to a railway`
         OR c's `did or caused to be done any other matter or thing`)
    AND c's `intended to endanger the safety of a person travelling or being upon the railway`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 32 (src:53)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 32: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 32 (src:53)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 32: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 33: casting stone, &c. upon a railway carriage, with intent to endanger the safety of any person therein`

-- src:54 | 33 Casting stone, &c. upon a railway carriage, with intent to endanger the safety of any person therein.
-- src:55 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously throw, or cause to fall or strike, at, against, into, or upon any engine, tender, carriage, or truck used upon any railway, any wood, stone, or other matter or thing, with intent to injure or endanger the safety of any person being in or upon such engine, tender, carriage, or truck, or in or upon any other engine, tender, carriage, or truck of any train of which such first-mentioned engine, tender, carriage, or truck shall form part, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude for life . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 33 (src:54-55)
-- The thing is thrown, or caused to fall or strike, at, against, into or upon an
-- engine, tender, carriage or truck used upon any railway (or another in the same
-- train as the one with a person in it), "with intent to injure or endanger the
-- safety of any person" in or upon it.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 33` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `threw, or caused to fall or strike, at, against, into or upon an engine, tender, carriage or truck used upon a railway, wood, stone or another matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to injure a person in or upon that engine, tender, carriage or truck, or another in the same train` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to endanger the safety of a person in or upon that engine, tender, carriage or truck, or another in the same train` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 33 (src:55)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 33`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND c's `threw, or caused to fall or strike, at, against, into or upon an engine, tender, carriage or truck used upon a railway, wood, stone or another matter or thing`
    AND (   c's `intended to injure a person in or upon that engine, tender, carriage or truck, or another in the same train`
         OR c's `intended to endanger the safety of a person in or upon that engine, tender, carriage or truck, or another in the same train`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 33 (src:55)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 33: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 33 (src:55)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 33: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 34: doing or omitting anything to endanger passengers by railway`

-- src:56 | 34 Doing or omitting anything to endanger passengers by railway.
-- src:57 | Whosoever, by any unlawful act, or by any wilful omission or neglect, shall endanger or cause to be endangered the safety of any person conveyed or being in or upon a railway, or shall aid or assist therein, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding two years, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 34 (src:56-57)
-- The means (either): "any unlawful act", or "any wilful omission or neglect".  The
-- result (either): endangering, or causing to be endangered, the safety of any person
-- conveyed or being in or upon a railway; or aiding or assisting "therein".  Nothing
-- in the text requires malice or intent.  FORK (see NOTES.md): "wilful" is read as
-- governing both "omission" and "neglect".
DECLARE `Conduct under section 34` HAS
    `did an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wilfully omitted or neglected to do something` IS A BOOLEAN
    `endangered, or caused to be endangered, the safety of a person conveyed or being in or upon a railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aided or assisted in endangering that safety` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 34 (src:57)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 34`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34: endangering railway passengers` c MEANS
        (   c's `did an unlawful act`
         OR c's `wilfully omitted or neglected to do something`)
    AND (   c's `endangered, or caused to be endangered, the safety of a person conveyed or being in or upon a railway`
         OR c's `aided or assisted in endangering that safety`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 34 (src:57)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 34: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

-- "liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding
-- two years": 24 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 34 (src:57)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 34: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 35: drivers of carriages injuring persons by furious driving`

-- src:58 | 35 Drivers of carriages injuring persons by furious driving.
-- src:59 | Whosoever, having the charge of any carriage or vehicle, shall by wanton or furious driving or racing, or other wilful misconduct, or by wilful neglect, do or cause to be done any bodily harm to any person whatsoever, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding two years, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 35 (src:58-59)
-- "having the charge of any carriage or vehicle", then doing or causing any bodily
-- harm to any person whatsoever by (any of): wanton or furious driving or racing;
-- other wilful misconduct; wilful neglect.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 35` HAS
    `had the charge of a carriage or vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `drove wantonly or furiously, or raced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed other wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was guilty of wilful neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did or caused to be done bodily harm to a person by it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 35 (src:59)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 35`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` c MEANS
        c's `had the charge of a carriage or vehicle`
    AND (   c's `drove wantonly or furiously, or raced`
         OR c's `committed other wilful misconduct`
         OR c's `was guilty of wilful neglect`)
    AND c's `did or caused to be done bodily harm to a person by it`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 35 (src:59)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 35: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 35 (src:59)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 35: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)
